; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5843  \DESCRIPTION Access to Nm_GetNmBusNmAssociation<BusNm>BusNmChannelIndexToBusNmIndexIndirections table to get the number of BusNm 
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5844               used by Nm_BusNmSpecificPduRxIndication, created by the ComStackLib. 
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5845               The index Nm_GetSysToNmChInd(nmNetworkHandle) or nmNetworkHandle validity is proven in Nm_BusNmSpecificPduRxIndication. 
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5846  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The called function ensures that the passed calculated BusNm index is valid. 
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5847  
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5848   SBSW_JUSTIFICATION_END */
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5849  
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5850  /*
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5851  \CM CM_NMIF_GENERAL_FUNCTIONCALL The parameters are not used in address calculations for memory manipulating
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5852                                   operations. Such calculations include but are not limited to: Array indexing,
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5853                                   pointer offset calculation and related forms of pointer arithmetic. Furthermore
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5854                                   these parameters are not forwarded to other software modules which could use
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5855                                   them for such operations unless they implement appropriate countermeasures.
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5856                                   And the addresses in the pointer variables are not saved in global variables
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5857                                   so that they could be used outside the function call. In that case, they are no
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5858                                   longer valid.
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5859  */
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5860  
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5861  /* COV_JUSTIFICATION_BEGIN
; ..\BSW\Nm\Nm.c	  5862  
